The phone agent for FreyaBank-Ekstre-Borc is built, saved under slot `final-freyabank-ekstre-borc`, and passed 9 of 9 simulated calls on the second test run. The first run passed 6 of 9.

**What it does:**
- **Card choice:** it loads the caller's cards without asking for the customer number. If there are several cards, it asks which one, using at most two of the caller's own card names as examples. Two cards with the same name are told apart by asking for the last four digits, then the last six, then the full number.
- **Reading the debt:** every sentence is built in code, so the model never composes figures. Amounts are spoken in Turkish words, currencies always by full name ("İngiliz Sterlini", never "GBP"), and card digits one by one, never more than the last four. Amounts and dates for all six example scenarios match what the examples expect.
- **Follow-ups:**
  - **Other cards:** a caller with more than one card is asked "Başka bir kartınızın borcunu…" before the offer.
  - **Offer:** it only includes what the caller can use; e-mail is left out when the bank has no address on file.
  - **Statement week:** the new dates are read first and the change waits for a clear "evet". A hedged "olur herhalde" is asked again, and the change runs only once.
  - **E-mail:** the statement goes only to the registered address, and "gönderildi" is said only after the service confirms it.
- **Endings:**
  - **To the main menu:** no eligible card, three failed tries, out-of-scope questions (asked first), a request about someone else's card, and a caller not speaking Turkish.
  - **To a human agent:** service errors, payment requests, disputes, and an explicit request for a person.
  - **After calming:** an angry caller gets up to three calming replies before being transferred.
- **Conflicts between documents:** I followed the newest decision each time (for example, three calming replies rather than one, and asking before sending out-of-scope callers to the main menu). Each conflict and the version chosen is listed in the facts file.

**Fixes after the first run:**
- Clearing the customer's previous answer with an empty value was silently rejected by the platform, so I clear it with a neutral value instead.
- A 404 from the card list skips the response hook. The agent now reads it from the platform's own error fields, so "no eligible card" goes to the main menu instead of to an agent.
- The interrupt handlers (pay, agent, out of scope and so on) only fire while the agent is waiting for the caller. Before, the out-of-scope one hijacked a statement-week change.

**Not built:**
- **Silence handling:** the three-silences hang-up isn't built, because the workflow format has no silence signal.
- **Currency moved into Turkish Lira:** there is no sentence for this, because the bank's documents never wrote one and no test card has the case.
- **Once-a-year limit:** the week change is always offered, because no service says whether the caller has already used this year's change.

All seven tools call `https://freya-bank-mock.pages-placeholder.workers.dev/voice/v1/<service>`, and the file contains no tunnel URLs.

